 radius $4$ centered at $(0,0).$ \n\nCartesian and polar coordinates are connected by the following equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's now write our curves in polar coordinates.\n\n- For ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=16,$ we obtain $r=4.$\n\n- For $x=2\\sqrt{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =2\\sqrt{2} \\\\ r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =2\\sqrt{2} \\\\ r & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta } \\\\ r & =2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's find the limits for the parameter $\\theta .$ Our curves intersect at the point $(2\\sqrt{2},2\\sqrt{2}).$ So, the entire region $D$ lies between the polar lines $\\theta =0$ and $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{4},$ as depicted below.  \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056707/assets/375e270ce444d9f62b50f9a25abfae781113fdad895833d693061ffffe93f5d3.png)\n\nAs a result, the region can be expressed in polar coordinates $(r,\\theta )$ as \n\n$$\nΔ={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta \\le r\\le 4,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{4}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\frac{6x}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{Δ}\\frac{6r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{{r}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{r}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,r\\,\\text{d}r\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}{\\int }_{2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta }^{4}6\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}6\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta {\\int }_{2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta }^{4}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}6\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta [r]_{2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta }^{4}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}6\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta (4-2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}(24\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -12\\sqrt{2})\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =[24\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -12\\sqrt{2}\\,\\theta ]_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =[(24\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})-12\\sqrt{2}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}))-0] \\\\  & =12\\sqrt{2}-3\\pi \\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535150 true] [17592186334036 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334037 13194139535150 true] [17592186334036 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334038 13194139535150 true] [17592186334036 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334039 13194139535150 true] [17592186334036 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334040 13194139535150 true] [17592186334036 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334041 13194139535150 true] [17592186334036 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535150 true] [17592186334036 1041 "selection" 13194139535150 true] [17592186334036 1104 #edb/ref 17592186334039 13194139535150 true] [17592186334036 1110 #uuid "94034ac5-6db5-5120-a36f-bd11e45979ae" 13194139535150 true] [17592186334037 1034 "12\\pi " 13194139535150 true] [17592186334037 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535150 true] [17592186334037 1111 #uuid "ddacb08e-ad82-53d2-ac7f-c049bc330e86" 13194139535150 true] [17592186334038 1034 "3\\sqrt{2}+5" 13194139535150 true] [17592186334038 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535150 true] [17592186334038 1111 #uuid "c36785ed-045f-51a6-8b92-9a58654176bd" 13194139535150 true] [17592186334039 1034 "12\\sqrt{2}-3\\pi \\sqrt{2}" 13194139535150 true] [17592186334039 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535150 true] [17592186334039 1111 #uuid "d5d79de3-7bb2-5eda-9290-1df112a63404" 13194139535150 true] [17592186334040 1034 "\\pi \\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{3}" 13194139535150 true] [17592186334040 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535150 true] [17592186334040 1111 #uuid "8d38fea8-c8fe-5682-b61d-6d4a9ac0ab12" 13194139535150 true] [17592186334041 1034 "12\\pi \\sqrt{2}" 13194139535150 true] [17592186334041 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535150 true] [17592186334041 1111 #uuid "422b5cf8-a06b-5621-b3c8-3d63da0bb4fe" 13194139535150 true] [17592186334042 1017 #edb/ref 17592186334043 13194139535150 true] [17592186334042 1089 "q-85206" 13194139535150 true] [17592186334042 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535150 true] [17592186334042 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056707/assets/bf7089294bc72330065590a9fe54acebee6d0ab982bffb4a162407c7232898ec.png)\n\nEvaluate the double integral ${∬}_{D}\\frac{4y}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A,$ where the region $D$ is shown above." 13194139535150 true] [17592186334042 1113 #uuid "3911b601-a237-5fb0-be5d-bd15dffefda8" 13194139535150 true] [17592186334042 1145 "We need to change the coordinate system from Cartesian coordinates to polar coordinates. To do this, we will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }dA={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\text{ }drd\\theta .\n$$\n\nNotice that the region $D$ represents a portion of the disk of radius $1$ centered at $(0,1).$ \n\nCartesian and polar coordinates are connected by the following equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's now write our curves in polar coordinates.\n\n- For ${x}^{2}+(y-1)^{2}=1,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+(y-1)^{2} & =1 \\\\ (r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}+(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -1)^{2} & =1 \\\\ {r}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{r}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta -2r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +1 & =1 \\\\ {r}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )-2r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & =0 \\\\ {r}^{2}-2r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & =0 \\\\ r(r-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nSince $r$ cannot be identical to zero on the entire semicircle, we must have $r=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .$\n\n- For $y=1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =1 \\\\ r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & =1 \\\\ r & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } \\\\ r & =\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's find the limits for the parameter $\\theta .$ Our curves intersect at the point $(-1,1).$ So, the entire region $D$ lies between the polar lines $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and $\\theta =\\frac{3\\pi }{4},$ as depicted below.  \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056707/assets/1b83e2674bba4bd6c326083f8c94496b5288de23575dc63a92b9a660eba69f67.png)\n\nAs a result, the region can be expressed in polar coordinates $(r,\\theta )$ as \n\n$$\nΔ={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta \\le r\\le 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{3\\pi }{4}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\frac{4y}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{Δ}\\frac{4r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{{r}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{r}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,r\\,\\text{d}r\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /4}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta }^{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /4}4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta {\\int }_{\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta }^{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /4}4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta [r]_{\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta }^{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /4}4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta (2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /4}(2{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta -1)\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =-4{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =-2[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )]_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /4} \\\\  & =-2[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )] \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535150 true] [17592186334043 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334044 13194139535150 true] [17592186334043 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334045 13194139535150 true] [17592186334043 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334046 13194139535150 true] [17592186334043 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334047 13194139535150 true] [17592186334043 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334048 13194139535150 true] [17592186334043 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535150 true] [17592186334043 1041 "selection" 13194139535150 true] [17592186334043 1104 #edb/ref 17592186334048 13194139535150 true] [17592186334043 1110 #uuid "fa4b75d4-b828-549b-b05e-2d2e1004592c" 13194139535150 true] [17592186334044 1034 "2\\sqrt{3}" 13194139535150 true] [17592186334044 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535150 true] [17592186334044 1111 #uuid "155180f4-d19a-5aff-9529-b2cde64bd4c1" 13194139535150 true] [17592186334045 1034 "2-\\pi " 13194139535150 true] [17592186334045 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535150 true] [17592186334045 1111 #uuid "2f112108-fc29-5944-b533-b4da8475ffb3" 13194139535150 true] [17592186334046 1034 "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\pi " 13194139535150 true] [17592186334046 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535150 true] [17592186334046 1111 #uuid "c08bf500-b4aa-54f9-a809-fb58f01d0092" 13194139535150 true] [17592186334047 1034 "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" 13194139535150 true] [17592186334047 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535150 true] [17592186334047 1111 #uuid "bfc8ba26-c416-5083-b24b-b9e2a596de61" 13194139535150 true] [17592186334048 1034 "2" 13194139535150 true] [17592186334048 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535150 true] [17592186334048 1111 #uuid "f02dd304-8613-5e88-a981-a78f6e4032b8" 13194139535150 true]] :edb/tempids {"q-161079" 17592186333965 "q-161079/selection" 17592186333966 "q-161079/selection/2112bfb200189d6e5ae9008492861cac8c419062b1ec6c71bc74d6293c8635e9" 17592186333967 "q-161079/selection/602b414e82fcea386986e76d3a19f34e5